---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="THE ENERGY OF MEMORY — Hyperarchiviation Studies">
  <article class="energy-study">
    <nav class="study-top" aria-label="Research navigation"><a href={base+'otherwise-hyperarchive/'}>← HYPERARCHIVIATION STUDIES / EMAP</a><span>RESEARCH STUDY 001 / 2027</span></nav>
    <header class="study-hero"><p class="eyebrow">OTHERWISE HYPERARCHIVE / INFRASTRUCTURE STUDIES</p><h1>THE ENERGY<br/>OF MEMORY<span class="accent">_</span></h1><p class="lead">Who powers, owns and maintains our collective digital memory?</p><p class="meta">ENERGY ★ INFRASTRUCTURE ★ OWNERSHIP ★ AUTONOMY ★ CARE</p></header>
    <nav class="study-nav" aria-label="Sections"><a href="#question">01 QUESTION</a><a href="#atlas">02 ATLAS</a><a href="#sustainability">03 SUSTAINABILITY</a><a href="#cases">04 CASES</a><a href="#prototype">05 PROTOTYPE</a><a href="#sources">06 SOURCES</a></nav>
    <section id="question"><span class="index">01 / RESEARCH QUESTION</span><div><h2>Keeping memory <em>alive.</em></h2><p>Digital archives are often described as immaterial spaces of preservation. Yet their continuity depends on electricity, hardware, networks, maintenance labour, service providers and contracts. How do these dependencies shape which collective memories remain accessible?</p><p>This study extends Hyperarchiviation Studies through an inquiry into the ecological, economic and political conditions of independent archives. Rather than presuming that self-hosting is automatically sustainable, it asks what autonomy costs and who bears that cost.</p></div></section>
    <section id="atlas"><span class="index">02 / INFRASTRUCTURE ATLAS</span><div><h2>Who hosts <em>the archive?</em></h2><p>Map the visible and obscured relations between cultural archives, social platforms, cloud providers, content delivery networks, data centres, energy suppliers and governing entities.</p><div class="matrix"><div><small>INPUT</small><strong>ARCHIVE / PLATFORM</strong><p>Storage, publication, access and preservation practices.</p></div><div><small>DEPENDENCY</small><strong>HOST / NETWORK / POWER</strong><p>Known suppliers, ownership and maintenance relationships.</p></div><div><small>OUTPUT</small><strong>ACCESS / CONTINUITY</strong><p>Who can modify, withdraw, migrate or switch off the archive?</p></div></div><p class="note">RESEARCH RULE / A missing disclosure is recorded as unknown, never silently replaced with an estimate.</p></div></section>
    <section id="sustainability"><span class="index">03 / SUSTAINABILITY STUDIES</span><div><h2>What does <em>continuity cost?</em></h2><p>Compare commercial hosting, dedicated self-hosting and shared community infrastructure. Include operational electricity, hardware lifecycle and embodied impacts, cooling and water where available, network transfer, maintenance time, financial cost and access governance.</p><div class="matrix"><div><small>SCENARIO A</small><strong>COMMERCIAL CLOUD</strong><p>Shared infrastructure; limited service-level energy transparency.</p></div><div><small>SCENARIO B</small><strong>SELF-HOSTED NODE</strong><p>Directly measurable electricity; responsibility for hardware and uptime.</p></div><div><small>SCENARIO C</small><strong>COMMUNITY HOSTING</strong><p>Shared maintenance and governance; negotiated resource use.</p></div></div><p class="note">METHOD / Distinguish measured values, provider-reported values, modelled estimates and unavailable data. Avoid equating total corporate energy use with the energy cost of a single archive.</p></div></section>
    <section id="cases"><span class="index">04 / COMPARATIVE CASES</span><div><h2>Different scales / <em>different dependencies.</em></h2><div class="cases"><div><small>CASE 001</small><h3>Internet Archive</h3><p>Long-term digital preservation, storage strategy and operational continuity.</p></div><div><small>CASE 002</small><h3>Wikimedia</h3><p>Non-profit infrastructure, hosting governance and public access.</p></div><div><small>CASE 003</small><h3>Commercial platforms</h3><p>Corporate energy reporting, cloud supply chains and control of user archives.</p></div><div><small>CASE 004</small><h3>Independent archives</h3><p>Small-scale hosting, collective maintenance and situated sustainability.</p></div></div><p>These are starting points for investigation, not completed audits. Provider relationships and consumption figures require dated primary sources and clearly stated reporting boundaries.</p></div></section>
    <section id="prototype"><span class="index">05 / ARTISTIC PROTOTYPE</span><div><h2>The living <em>archive.</em></h2><p>Experiment with a functioning sculptural server hosting a portion of a collective archive. Meter its electricity consumption and expose the maintenance, interruptions and decisions usually hidden behind a continuously available interface.</p><div class="diagram" role="img" aria-label="Diagram connecting collective contributions to a measurable server and a public archive"><div>COLLECTIVE<br/>CONTRIBUTIONS</div><b>→</b><div class="core">LIVING SERVER<br/><small>POWER METER / STORAGE</small></div><b>→</b><div>PUBLIC ARCHIVE<br/>INTERFACE</div></div><p>What might be learned by comparing a directly measured small archive with the partial disclosures of much larger platforms? How can an archive remain accessible without reproducing the infrastructures it questions?</p></div></section>
    <section id="sources"><span class="index">06 / SOURCES & PROTOCOLS</span><div><h2>An open <em>research ledger.</em></h2><p>Next steps: collect sustainability reports, public infrastructure documentation, relevant European data-centre research and hosting invoices or measurements from the prototype. Each future dataset should record its source, date, scope, unit, method, uncertainty and licensing.</p><p class="note">STATUS / RESEARCH FRAMEWORK — DATA COLLECTION AND VERIFICATION PENDING.</p><p><a href={base+'otherwise-hyperarchive/'}>← BACK TO HYPERARCHIVIATION STUDIES / EMAP</a></p></div></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.energy-study{--line:rgba(128,128,128,.4);--signal:#39ff14;font-family:Helvetica,"Helvetica Neue",Arial,sans-serif;max-width:1500px;margin:auto;padding:20px clamp(18px,4vw,64px) 100px;color:inherit}.energy-study a{color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.energy-study a:hover{color:var(--signal)}.study-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;font-size:10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:10px 0}.study-hero{padding:65px 0 55px}.eyebrow,.meta,.index,.study-nav,.note,.matrix small,.cases small{font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.035em}.study-hero h1{font-size:clamp(46px,10vw,150px);line-height:.88;letter-spacing:-.075em;margin:35px 0;font-weight:700}.accent{color:var(--signal)}.lead{font-size:clamp(19px,3vw,38px);max-width:780px;line-height:1.15}.meta{margin-top:35px}.study-nav{display:flex;gap:24px;overflow-x:auto;white-space:nowrap;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:17px 0}.energy-study section{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(140px,25%) minmax(0,1fr);gap:20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:48px 0}.energy-study section>div{min-width:0}.energy-study h2{font-size:clamp(27px,4.4vw,62px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.055em;margin:0 0 28px}.energy-study h2 em{font-family:Georgia,"Times New Roman",serif;font-weight:400;color:#ff2bbd}.energy-study p{max-width:850px;line-height:1.55}.matrix,.cases{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));margin:30px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-left:1px solid var(--line)}.matrix>div,.cases>div{padding:18px;border-right:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.matrix small,.cases small{display:block;color:var(--signal);margin-bottom:18px}.matrix strong{font-size:13px}.matrix p,.cases p{font-size:12px}.cases{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.cases h3{font-size:18px}.note{border-left:2px solid var(--signal);padding:12px 16px;margin:22px 0}.diagram{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:22px;margin:28px 0;font-size:11px;text-align:center}.diagram>div{flex:1;padding:24px 8px;border:1px solid var(--line)}.diagram>.core{border-color:var(--signal)}.diagram b{color:var(--signal)}.diagram small{font-size:9px}@media(max-width:700px){.energy-study section{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px;padding:32px 0}.study-hero{padding:38px 0}.matrix,.cases{grid-template-columns:1fr}.study-top{flex-wrap:wrap}.diagram{gap:5px;padding:10px;font-size:9px}.diagram>div{padding:12px 3px}.diagram small{font-size:7px}}
</style>